  "side_hold": "A same-controller latch remembers the first 1.0-1.6-pixel spatial pass side when its three road rows give at least 2.0-pixel width and a 0.8-pixel advantage. After that plan disappears, it keeps at least 0.07 steer toward the same obstacle side until bbox bottom exceeds row 52 while the width advantage persists. Track 2/2570310388 and track 4/1402259577 changed from DNF to finish; other seven tested cells kept exact frozen action hashes, including two candidate-only gains and three shared finishes. A no-op baseline replay exactly matched the candidate cold-worker action hash on track 2/2570310388.",
  "decision": "PROMISING_DEVELOPMENT_ONLY",
  "limits": "The side-hold arm band (bbox bottom 24-30, initial observation, 1.0-1.6-pixel margin) was selected after inspecting consumed screen failures and is not a generalization claim. Two of four contact losses remain unchanged, and the contact-free road-exit loss was not part of this nine-cell comparison. This probe cannot override the rejected v1 screen, unlock its sealed confirmation or blind cells, or justify activation. Test a coherent source on broader consumed geometries, then preregister independent fresh geometry and gates. Linux submission-container certification remains outstanding."
